# SRG-APP-000835-WSR-000200  -  CAT II
# The web server must, for password-based authentication, update the list of
# passwords on an organization-defined frequency.
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations, then kept
# by hand. Edit this file to change how this requirement is assessed here;
# it is read at run time. Regenerating refreshes the benchmark text in place
# and leaves the criteria, the determination and any verification block as
# they are.

id:              SRG-APP-000835-WSR-000200
group:           V-264346
severity:        medium
cat:             CAT II
determination:   ORGANIZATIONAL
grade:           D
decidable:       manual
confidence:      derived
cci:             CCI-004059
control_rev5:    IA-5

contribution:    None, and the web tier adds nothing: Splunk Web authenticates through
                 authentication.conf and the product holds no password deny list to update,
                 nor any setting expressing an update frequency for one.

external:        Updating the list on the organization-defined frequency - carried by
                 organizational policy.
external:        Holding and refreshing the list used to screen web-tier logins - carried
                 by the directory service or identity provider, or by a proxy that fronts
                 Splunk Web.

manual_reason:   No conf key expresses the list or the frequency of its update, so no
                 observed configuration value can decide this requirement; the frequency is
                 organization-defined.

citation:        splunk-spec-files/authentication.conf.spec:437-600;
                 splunk-spec-files/web.conf.spec:16
finding:         Not a finding against the application: the product holds no password deny
                 list for the web tier to update and has no setting for an update
                 frequency, so this requirement is carried by organizational policy and the
                 identity provider; this determination is from the perspective of the
                 application layer alone.
